    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0390" n="310" xml:id="pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Mutual Guarantee (Locarno)/691:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-22T16:00:00+01:00">May 22, 1936—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—11:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275. With reference to penultimate paragraph of my 270, May 20, 12 noon, I was
                    informed by a reliable source that information has reached this country during
                    the last day or so that <hi rendition="#italic">pourparlers</hi> have indirectly
                    been opened by Hitler with Mussolini, the former stressing the preeminence of
                    the German minority question in Czechoslovakia and that the friendship of Italy
                    was more important to Germany than Austria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
